.TH ZLINUXDOCS 1 "2026" "zlinuxdocs @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zlinuxdocs, zld \- inspect, repair, convert and validate .docx document sets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zlinuxdocs
.I COMMAND
[\fIFILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B zld
.I COMMAND
[\fIFILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zlinuxdocs
is for people who are sent Word documents and have to turn them into PDFs that
will not be handed back at the counter.
.PP
Run
.B zlinuxdocs quickstart
for a five-command walkthrough that uses the example documents installed at
.IR /usr/share/zlinuxdocs/samples/ ,
so it works before you have a file of your own.
.PP
.B zld
is a short alias for
.BR zlinuxdocs .
The two are the same program.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect \fIFILE.docx\fR
Say what is really inside a Word document: paragraphs, tables, real headings,
look-alike headings and [V] markers. Read-only.
Also written as \fBinfo\fR or \fBshow\fR.
.TP
.B fix\-headings \fIFILE.docx\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUT.docx\fR
Turn text that only looks like a heading ("1 - Introduction", "2.1 Scope",
"ANNEXURE III") into a real heading carrying an outline level, which is what
makes bookmarks appear in an exported PDF. Idempotent: a second run reports
0 promotions. Never overwrites the input unless \fB\-\-in\-place\fR is given,
and never replaces an existing output without \fB\-\-force\fR.
Also written as \fBfix\fR or \fBrepair\fR.
.TP
.B convert \fIFILE\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUT.pdf\fR
Make a PDF through LibreOffice with bookmarks and a searchable text layer.
Can also produce .docx, .odt, .txt or .html; giving an old .doc file and an
\fB\-o\fR ending in .docx modernises it. Requires the
.B libreoffice\-writer
package.
Also written as \fBpdf\fR or \fBto\-pdf\fR.
.TP
.B validate \fIFILE.pdf\fR
Check the PDF has pages, bookmarks, selectable text, no leftover Word field
codes and a sound internal structure. Exits non-zero when any check fails, so
it can gate a script. Read-only.
Also written as \fBcheck\fR or \fBverify\fR.
.TP
.B markers \fIFILE.docx\fR
List the [V] verification marks a reviewer left behind, in paragraphs and
inside table cells. Read-only.
Also written as \fBflags\fR or \fBtodo\fR.
.TP
.B profile
Show or export the house print settings (paper, margins, fonts, contents page,
PDF options). Also written as \fBsettings\fR.
.TP
.B quickstart
A numbered, copy-pasteable walkthrough using the shipped examples.
.TP
.B examples
Real command lines you can copy and paste.
.TP
.B samples
List the example documents installed with the program.
.SH OPTIONS
Each command has its own options; run
.B zlinuxdocs help \fICOMMAND\fR
to see them. Common ones:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Say what would happen and write nothing. Available on every command that writes.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow an existing output file to be replaced. Without it, an existing output is
never overwritten.
.TP
.B \-\-in\-place
Replace the original file. A .bak copy is kept beside it.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Show the technical detail. The default output stays plain.
.TP
.B \-\-examples
Print example command lines for that command and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. For
.BR validate ,
the PDF passed every check.
.TP
.B 1
The command could not do what was asked, or
.B validate
found a problem. A plain-language explanation is printed to standard error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was not understood (unknown command, missing argument).
.TP
.B 3
The program's own files are missing; reinstall the package.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B python3
and
.B poppler\-utils
are required. Install
.B libreoffice\-writer
to use
.BR convert ,
and
.B qpdf
for the deep structural check in
.BR validate .
The Python libraries python-docx, PyYAML and pypdf are vendored under
.I /usr/share/zlinuxdocs/vendor/
and are not taken from the system.
.SH PDF/A
.B PDF/A conformance is not claimed.
.B convert \-\-pdfa
asks LibreOffice for an archival flavour, but nothing in this program can
verify conformance; that needs a dedicated validator such as veraPDF. Do not
describe output from this program as certified PDF/A.
.SH PRIVACY
This program makes no network connections and collects no telemetry. Your
documents never leave the machine. The package installs no maintainer scripts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/zlinuxdocs/samples/
Example documents. See the README.md beside them.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zlinuxdocs/profiles/house_profile.yaml
The house print profile.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zlinuxdocs/vendor/
Vendored Python libraries and their licences.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
cd /tmp
cp "/usr/share/zlinuxdocs/samples/plain-no-headings.docx" "My Report.docx"
zlinuxdocs inspect      "My Report.docx"
zlinuxdocs fix-headings "My Report.docx" -o "My Report (fixed).docx"
zlinuxdocs convert      "My Report (fixed).docx" -o "My Report.pdf"
zlinuxdocs validate     "My Report.pdf"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soffice (1),
.BR pdfinfo (1),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR qpdf (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/zexp1/zlinuxdocs/issues
